package com.yourcompany.project.service.ruleengine.spi;
import com.yourcompany.project.service.ruleengine.core.RuleTargetGroup;
import java.util.List;

public interface RuleProvider {
    // e.g., loadRulesForTable("DISPOSITION_MASTER")
    List<RuleTargetGroup> loadRulesForTable(String targetTable); 
}
The Calling Application (Bridging Engine Output to Master Data)
When your application service calls the Rule Engine, it uses the targetPk returned by the engine to fetch the rich details from your existing Master tables.

Java
@Service
public class AssessmentService {

    private final RuleEngine dispositionEngine;
    private final DispositionMasterRepository dispositionRepo; // Your existing JPA Repo

    public AssessmentService(RuleProvider ruleProvider, DispositionMasterRepository dispositionRepo) {
        this.dispositionRepo = dispositionRepo;
        // Initialize engine with only rules pointing to DISPOSITION_MASTER
        this.dispositionEngine = new RuleEngine(ruleProvider.loadRulesForTable("DISPOSITION_MASTER"));
    }

    public AssessmentResponse evaluatePia(Map<String, List<String>> facts) {
        List<EvaluationResult> ruleResults = dispositionEngine.process(facts);
        
        List<String> finalDispositions = new ArrayList<>();
        
        for (EvaluationResult result : ruleResults) {
            // Use the returned PK to fetch the existing Master Record
            Long masterPk = Long.valueOf(result.getTargetPk());
            
            dispositionRepo.findById(masterPk).ifPresent(masterRecord -> {
                // Log justification, map master data, etc.
                System.out.println("Triggered: " + masterRecord.getName() + " | Reason: " + result.getJustification());
                finalDispositions.add(masterRecord.getName());
            });
        }
        
        return new AssessmentResponse(finalDispositions);
    }
}
5. Summary of Architecture Benefits
Zero Duplication: Your engine strictly manages logic, while your application strictly manages master data.

Highly Reusable: If a new team wants to use the engine for FRAUD_ALERT_MASTER, they simply insert rules with TARGET_TABLE = 'FRAUD_ALERT_MASTER' and map their PKs. The pure Java engine requires zero code changes.

Library Ready: This package (com.yourcompany.project.service.ruleengine) is entirely self-contained and ready to be compiled into a standalone .jar file whenever required.
